; rds_dec.loom
; RDS / RBDS (IEC 62106, NRSC-4) decoder at baseband: the biphase-coded
; data signal from a 57 kHz demodulator's data slicer on IN0. Recovers the
; bit clock, undoes the biphase and the differential coding, finds the
; blocks by syndrome, corrects bursts, and reports every block to the host
; through OUTQ[1] with the name of its offset word.
;
; Written on 2026-11-26, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035): RDS is in no design
; document. Hardware reused from other jobs: the level and edge waits
; (`WAITE ... T`, built for the serial receivers) time the line; the tick
; restart on a TICK_INT write (SEMANTICS 4, built for UART start bits) is
; the clock recovery; `IN` reads the line; `LD`/`ST` (SEMANTICS 6.11,
; D-027, built for device emulation) hold the state and the tables. The
; bit engine does not help here (its SHI shifts pin levels, and an RDS
; bit is the XOR of two consecutive levels; its CRC unit keeps a running
; remainder, not the remainder of a 26-bit window). What the firmware does
; that no hardware does: the clock recovery and the biphase decision, the
; differential decoding, the syndrome of the last 26 bits at every bit,
; block and group synchronisation with no sync word, burst-error
; correction by error trapping, loss of sync, and the reports.
;
; Clock recovery: a tick is a sixteenth of a bit. Biphase has an edge in
; the middle of every bit (NRSC-4-A 1.7). The thread watches the line from
; 14/16 to 20/16 of a bit after the last mid-bit edge (WAITE RXD, ANY, T);
; an edge restarts the tick grid and the line is sampled 4 ticks later,
; in the second half-symbol. No edge by 20/16 means the thread was
; following the edges between bits (a run of 0s has them too): it moves
; half a bit (SETD 8) and watches again, and a bit is lost; after start-up
; that happens at most once, at the first 1. The first edge after RUN is
; taken as a mid-bit edge. The bit clock is not a PLL: every bit is timed
; from its own mid-bit edge, so a rate error only moves the sample within
; the half-symbol (1 % is tested; BS.643-3 allows 0.0105 %).
;
; Decoding: the bit is this half-symbol's level XOR the last one's
; (1.6 Table 2: either polarity). The window of the last 26 bits is r1
; (bits 25..10 back, so at a block's end r1 is its information word) and
; r0[15:6] (the newest 10). Its remainder mod g(x) is kept in r2 at every
; bit: s = s x + d, reduced by
; g, and x^26 mod g = 0x0EE taken out when the bit 26 back is a 1. A clean
; block's remainder is its offset word (Annex A; Table B.1's syndromes
; are these times x^325 mod g: tools/protomodels/rds.py checks it).
;
; Synchronisation (Annex C C.1): searching, every bit position whose
; remainder is one of the five offset words is a candidate; the 26th bit
; after it must give an offset word that follows it in a group (A B C|C' D
; A); then the decoder is in sync and reports that second block. While a
; candidate waits its 26 bits, other matches are ignored; if it fails,
; the search goes on from that bit. In sync, every 26th bit ends a block:
; clean if the remainder is the expected offset (C or C' for block 3),
; otherwise the burst is searched for. LOSS (`cfg`, 8 in the image; C.1.2
; suggests deciding over up to 50 blocks) blocks in a row that are not
; clean lose sync, and the search starts again at the next bit.
;
; Burst correction (2.3: any single burst of span 5 or less; Annex B.2.2
; traps it in the syndrome register): t = remainder XOR offset is
; multiplied by x^-1 mod g (if odd, XOR g, then halve) for p = 0..21; the
; first t < 32 is the error t x^p, and its part in bits 25..10 is XORed
; into the information word. One step a bit, over the 22 bits after the
; block, so a corrected or bad block is reported up to 22 bits late. No
; t < 32 by p = 21: the block is bad (two bursts, or one longer than 5).
; Block 3's offset for the search is C' when the last block 2 that was not
; bad had B0 = 1 (NRSC-4-A 3.1.2).
;
; Host words (FIFO space, thread 1), two per block, nothing in INQ:
;   A: the information word (corrected if bit 3 of B is set);
;   B: 2:0 the offset (0 A, 1 B, 2 C, 3 C', 4 D; the expected one when the
;      block was not clean), 3 corrected, 4 bad (not correctable; A as
;      received), 5 overflow (reports were dropped before this one), 6
;      sync (the block that confirmed a candidate), 7 lost (sync lost
;      after this block). 15:8 zero.
;   A report whose A word finds OUTQ full is dropped and the next carries
;   the overflow bit; a B word that finds it full goes out at the next
;   bit with room, and reports made meanwhile are dropped.
;
; Tick (set by the host before RUN): 1/16 of a bit: 2631 + 148/256 at
; 50 MHz, 2368 + 108/256 at 45 MHz. The work is proved for ticks of 64
; clocks or more (.tick 64: 1024 clocks a bit).
;
; Registers: r0 r1 the window, r2 its remainder, r3 bits to the
; candidate's or the block's end, r5 flags (bit 0 the last level), r6 the
; offset the remainder matches (5: none), r4 r7 scratch. The rest is in
; `V` (data memory), placed before the code so every table address is a
; one-word MOV16.
;
; Size: 256 words, 0x080-0x17F: 218 of code and 38 of data (0x081-0x0A6).
; It fills thread 1's quarter and thread 2's, so thread 2 must not be
; started with this image; thread 3's quarter is free. With rds_enc.loom
; (0x000-0x074) the pair takes 359 of 512 words as threads 0 and 1. No CALL: the deadline checker returns a RET to
; every call site, so a subroutine called twice on one path would be a
; loop with no anchor. `--strict` and `--staged-edges`: two deadline pairs,
; the worst (the sample's WAITD 4 to the WAITD 10 that closes the bit's
; work) 128 slots, slack 128 clocks at the 64-clock tick; two `.bounded`
; PUSHes, each guarded by a `WAITB OUTQ_NF, T` just before it that
; completed with T = 0.

        .imem   512                     ; the macro build: quarters of 128 words
        .thread 1
        .pins   RXD = IN0
        .tick   64                      ; the shortest tick (1/16 bit) the work is proved for
        .equ    LEVEL = 1               ; r5: the last half-symbol level
        .equ    CAND = 2                ;   a candidate waits (searching)
        .equ    SYNC = 4                ;   in sync
        .equ    OWED = 8                ;   a report's B word waits for room
        .equ    TRAP = 16               ;   a burst search is running
        .equ    OVF = 32                ;   reports dropped (B bit 5)
        .equ    CORR = 8                ; B bits
        .equ    BAD = 16
        .equ    SYNCED = 64
        .equ    LOST = 128
        .equ    GX = 0x5B9              ; g(x) (2.3)
        .equ    GINV = GX >> 1          ; (t ^ g) >> 1 for odd t: t x^-1 mod g
        .equ    VT = 0                  ; fields of V (data memory)
        .equ    VP = 1
        .equ    VTINFO = 2
        .equ    VSTAT = 3
        .equ    VBRUN = 4
        .equ    VB0 = 5
        .equ    VCINFO = 6
        .equ    VOWED = 7
        .equ    VLOSS = 8
        .equ    VK = 9
        .equ    VCAND = 10

start:  JMP     init

; ------------------------------------------------------------ data (first, so a
; table's address is a one-word MOV16)
V:      .word   0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0  ; t, p, info, status, bad run, B0, -, owed B
cfg:    .word   8                       ; LOSS: blocks in a row not clean that lose sync
        .word   0, 0                    ; the block in the group, the candidate's offset
ht:     .word   0x17FF, 0x17FF, 0x0968, 0x17FF, 0x0F50, 0x11B4, 0x0598, 0x00FC
offs:   .word   0x0FC, 0x198, 0x168, 0x350, 0x1B4   ; A B C C' D (Annex A Table A.1)
nxt:    .word   0x02, 0x0C, 0x10, 0x10, 0x01        ; offsets that may follow, as bit masks
kn:     .word   1, 2, 3, 3, 0           ; the block in the group after that offset's
kx:     .word   0, 1, 2, 4              ; a block's offset: A B C D
km:     .word   0x01, 0x02, 0x0C, 0x10  ; the offsets a block may carry, as bit masks

init:   .csr    INGRP, 1 << 5 | pin(RXD)    ; IN reads RXD into bit 0
        LDI     r0, 0
        LDI     r1, 0
        LDI     r2, 0
        LDI     r5, 0
        WAITE   RXD, ANY                ; the first edge, taken as a mid-bit edge

; ------------------------------------------------------------ the bit clock
edge:   CSRR    r7, TICK_INT            ; restart the tick grid on the mid-bit edge
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r7
        SETD    0
        WAITD   4                       ; the second half-symbol
        IN      r7                      ; its level
        XOR     r7, r7, r5
        ANDI    r7, 1                   ; d = this level ^ the last (Table 2)
        XOR     r5, r5, r7              ; LEVEL = this level
        SHLI    r2, 1                   ; the remainder: s x + d mod g
        OR      r2, r2, r7
        MOV     r4, r2
        SHRI    r4, 10
        BZ      w0
        MOV16   r4, GX
        XOR     r2, r2, r4
w0:     SHLI    r1, 1                   ; C = the bit 26 back, leaving the window
        BNC     w1
        LDI     r4, 0xEE                ; x^26 mod g
        XOR     r2, r2, r4
w1:     SHLI    r0, 1                   ; C = the bit 10 back, into r1
        BNC     w2
        ORI     r1, 1
w2:     SHLI    r7, 6
        OR      r0, r0, r7              ; the new bit at r0[6]
        MOV     r7, r5                  ; an owed B word goes when OUTQ has room
        ANDI    r7, OWED
        BZ      w3
        WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T              ; a test: TD is reached
        BT      w3
        MOV16   r7, V
        LD      r7, r7, VOWED
        .bounded "the WAITB above completed with T = 0, so OUTQ had room in that slot's X cycle; only this thread pushes OUTQ[1] (SEMANTICS 6.7)"
        PUSH    r7
        XORI    r5, OWED
w3:     MOV     r7, r2                  ; r6 = the offset whose word the remainder is
        SHRI    r7, 2
        ANDI    r7, 7                   ; (bits 4:2 tell the five apart)
        MOV16   r4, ht
        ADD     r4, r4, r7
        LD      r4, r4, 0               ; that offset's word | its number << 10
        MOV     r6, r4
        SHRI    r6, 10
        XOR     r4, r4, r2
        SHLI    r4, 6                   ; Z = the low 10 bits are the remainder
        BZ      w4
        LDI     r6, 5                   ; none
w4:     MOV     r7, r5
        ANDI    r7, SYNC | CAND         ; (never both)
        BZ      hnew
        CMPI    r7, CAND
        BZ      hcand
        JMP     insync

; ------------------------------------------------------------ searching (C.1.1)
hnew:   CMPI    r6, 5
        BZ      tstep
        MOV16   r4, V                   ; a candidate: wait 26 bits
        ST      r6, r4, VCAND
        ORI     r5, CAND
        LDI     r3, 26
        JMP     tstep
hcand:  SUBI    r3, 1
        BNZ     tstep                   ; other matches meanwhile are ignored
        XORI    r5, CAND                ; the candidate's 26th bit:
        MOV16   r4, V
        LD      r4, r4, VCAND
        MOV16   r7, nxt
        ADD     r7, r7, r4
        LD      r7, r7, 0
        SHR     r7, r7, r6
        ANDI    r7, 1                   ; an offset that follows it in a group?
        BZ      hnew                    ; no: search on from this bit
        MOV16   r4, kn                  ; sync, on this block
        ADD     r4, r4, r6
        LD      r4, r4, 0
        MOV16   r7, V
        ST      r4, r7, VK              ; the next block in the group
        LDI     r4, 0
        ST      r4, r7, VBRUN
        ORI     r5, SYNC
        LDI     r3, 26
        LDI     r7, SYNCED
        OR      r7, r7, r6
        JMP     repw                    ; report it, flagged sync

; ------------------------------------------------------------ in sync: a block ends
insync: SUBI    r3, 1
        BNZ     tstep
        MOV16   r4, V
        LD      r7, r4, VK              ; r7 = the block in the group
        MOV     r3, r7
        ADDI    r3, 1
        ANDI    r3, 3
        ST      r3, r4, VK
        LDI     r3, 26
        MOV16   r4, km
        ADD     r4, r4, r7
        LD      r4, r4, 0
        SHR     r4, r4, r6
        ANDI    r4, 1                   ; an offset this block may carry (C or C')?
        BNZ     clean
        MOV16   r4, kx                  ; not clean: the expected offset
        ADD     r4, r4, r7
        CMPI    r7, 2
        LD      r7, r4, 0
        BNZ     dirty
        MOV16   r4, V
        LD      r4, r4, VB0
        ADD     r7, r7, r4              ; block 3 of a version B group: C'
dirty:  MOV16   r4, offs                ; t = remainder ^ expected offset word
        ADD     r4, r4, r7
        LD      r4, r4, 0
        XOR     r4, r4, r2
        MOV16   r6, V
        ST      r4, r6, VT
        ST      r7, r6, VSTAT
        LDI     r4, 0
        ST      r4, r6, VP
        ST      r1, r6, VTINFO          ; the information word as received
        LD      r4, r6, VBRUN
        ADDI    r4, 1
        ST      r4, r6, VBRUN
        LD      r7, r6, VLOSS
        CMP     r4, r7                  ; C = LOSS blocks in a row not clean
        BNC     dl
        LD      r4, r6, VSTAT
        LDI     r7, LOST
        OR      r4, r4, r7
        ST      r4, r6, VSTAT
        XORI    r5, SYNC                ; sync lost: search from the next bit
dl:     ORI     r5, TRAP                ; the burst search runs over the next bits
        JMP     done

; ------------------------------------------------------------ burst trapping (B.2.2)
; One step a bit: t x^p is the error if t < 32; else t <- t x^-1 mod g
; (if t is odd XOR g, then halve), p <- p + 1; p = 0..21 over 22 bits.
tstep:  MOV     r7, r5
        ANDI    r7, TRAP
        BZ      done
        MOV16   r6, V
        LD      r4, r6, VT
        CMPI    r4, 32
        BNC     tfound                  ; t < 32: a burst of span <= 5 at p
        SHRI    r4, 1                   ; C = t was odd
        BNC     t1
        MOV16   r7, GINV
        XOR     r4, r4, r7
t1:     ST      r4, r6, VT
        LD      r4, r6, VP
        ADDI    r4, 1
        ST      r4, r6, VP
        CMPI    r4, 22
        BNC     done                    ; p < 22: on at the next bit
        XORI    r5, TRAP                ; p = 0..21 tried: not correctable
        LD      r4, r6, VSTAT
        ORI     r4, BAD
        ST      r4, r6, VSTAT
        LD      r4, r6, VTINFO          ; as received
        JMP     rep
tfound: XORI    r5, TRAP
        LD      r7, r6, VP              ; the error is t x^p; its bits 25..10:
        CMPI    r7, 10
        BC      thi
        NEG     r7, r7
        ADDI    r7, 10
        SHR     r4, r4, r7              ; t >> (10 - p)
        JMP     tx
thi:    SUBI    r7, 10
        SHL     r4, r4, r7              ; t << (p - 10)
tx:     LD      r7, r6, VTINFO
        XOR     r4, r4, r7              ; the corrected information word
        LD      r7, r6, VSTAT
        ORI     r7, CORR
        ST      r7, r6, VSTAT
        JMP     rep

; ------------------------------------------------------------ reports
; clean: a block in sync that was clean (r6 its offset), then repw.
; repw: r7 = the status, the information word from the window (r1).
; rep: r4 = the information word, r6 = V, VSTAT the status.
clean:  MOV16   r4, V
        LDI     r7, 0
        ST      r7, r4, VBRUN
        MOV     r7, r6                  ; the status: the offset found
repw:   MOV16   r6, V
        ST      r7, r6, VSTAT
        MOV     r4, r1
rep:    LD      r7, r6, VSTAT           ; a block 2 (offset B), not bad: keep its B0
        ANDI    r7, 7 | BAD
        CMPI    r7, 1
        BNZ     rp
        MOV     r7, r4
        SHRI    r7, 11
        ANDI    r7, 1
        ST      r7, r6, VB0
rp:     MOV     r7, r5
        ANDI    r7, OWED
        BNZ     rdrop                   ; the last B still waits: drop this report
        WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T
        BT      rdrop
        .bounded "the WAITB above completed with T = 0, so OUTQ had room in that slot's X cycle; only this thread pushes OUTQ[1] (SEMANTICS 6.7)"
        PUSH    r4                      ; A
        LD      r7, r6, VSTAT
        MOV     r4, r5
        ANDI    r4, OVF
        OR      r7, r7, r4              ; B: the overflow bit, once
        XOR     r5, r5, r4
        ST      r7, r6, VOWED           ; B goes from the next bit on
        ORI     r5, OWED
        JMP     done
rdrop:  ORI     r5, OVF
done:   WAITD   10                      ; the work fits in 10 ticks: 14/16 after the edge
        SETD    6                       ; the next mid-bit edge is due at 16/16
watch:  WAITE   RXD, ANY, T
        BT      slip
        JMP     edge
slip:   SETD    8                       ; none by 20/16: half a bit off, look again
        JMP     watch
